turn_failed_note.empty_input:
Turn failed: {error}
This turn had no state to resume — the first model call never completed (common after an app restart or a failed first call).
Use retry on the error card; it re-runs the original input.

turn_failed_note.state:
Turn failed: {error}
A step hit inconsistent turn state — usually a checkpoint written by an older version or left mid-write by a crash.
Retry once; if it repeats, restart the app, then start a new session if it still repeats (traceback: ~/.ginno/logs/sidecar.log).

turn_failed_note.node_timeout:
Turn failed: {error}
A step exceeded its time budget — usually a slow provider or tool call, not a Ginno fault.
Retry; if it repeats, check the provider's status (traceback: ~/.ginno/logs/sidecar.log).

turn_failed_note.content_filter:
Turn failed: {error}
The provider's safety filter blocked the model's output while it was writing the answer — usually because a large amount of fetched material (many scraped pages, long documents) was summarized in one go.
Retrying the same request will be blocked the same way. Ask for a narrower slice (fewer pages, or summarize them in batches), and quote sources instead of pasting long passages.
